## 37. Important decisions before full implementation

There are three decisions that will materially affect the architecture.

Decision 1 — AI execution model

I recommend a hybrid model:

- Local models for privacy-sensitive processing where hardware permits.
- Hosted models for tasks requiring greater inference capability.
- Deterministic code for security policy, authorization and critical validation.

Do not make every security decision dependent on an LLM.

Decision 2 — Application architecture

Start with a modular monolith and separate background workers.

This is more manageable than deploying 15 independent microservices at the beginning. Preserve clear service boundaries so that individual components can be extracted later.

Decision 3 — Simulation before live operations

Start with synthetic telemetry, controlled simulation and test integrations. Connect actual organizational infrastructure only after authentication, permissions, monitoring and auditability have been validated.

